WEBVTT

00:00:01.331 --> 00:00:06.201
Yume kara samete mo
Even if I wake from my dreams

00:00:07.241 --> 00:00:12.701
Kono te wo nobasu yo
I'll reach my hand out to you

00:00:24.221 --> 00:00:29.491
Onaji tsuyosa de yobi au
If our hearts can reach each other

00:00:30.231 --> 00:00:34.861
Kokoro ni nareru no naraba
with the same strength

00:00:36.101 --> 00:00:41.361
Nanninbun no kizu demo
Then I would be able to bare

00:00:41.901 --> 00:00:47.031
Boku wa uketome rareru yo
The pain of many hearts

00:00:47.441 --> 00:00:51.041
Mousukoshi datte kiga surun da
I can feel that it will arrive soon

00:00:51.111 --> 00:00:55.981
Kono kabe ga kuzureru
When these walls will be torn down

00:00:56.791 --> 00:01:01.191
Reimei
The dawn

00:01:02.921 --> 00:01:08.891
Yume kara samete mo
mada minai yume no houmade
Even if we wake from our dreams
We'll have to keep running

00:01:08.961 --> 00:01:14.871
Bokura wa hitori de
hashiri tuzukeru shika nain da
Towards our unrevealed dreams

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:21.501
Korogari mayotte tsukuri dasu
boku no inryoku ga
The gravity by my painful journey
will draw me

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:27.721
Itsuka kimi e
To you one day

00:01:50.971 --> 00:01:55.841
I wonder what role
you're going to play.

00:02:04.291 --> 00:02:05.841
What was that for?!

00:02:06.551 --> 00:02:08.081
You're in the way.

00:02:09.391 --> 00:02:11.191
Hey, come over here.

00:02:13.801 --> 00:02:16.231
I'd rather stay over here.

00:02:19.031 --> 00:02:22.331
If you stand there, you'll get
in the way of people coming in.

00:02:23.101 --> 00:02:24.701
I can walk by myself.

00:02:27.381 --> 00:02:28.361
Okay, let's go!

00:02:29.611 --> 00:02:30.581
You know what?

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:32.981
What?

00:02:34.321 --> 00:02:37.581
Why did you guys join
this guild, anyway?

00:02:38.051 --> 00:02:39.081
Why?

00:02:39.321 --> 00:02:40.481
Because I was invited!

00:02:42.491 --> 00:02:45.391
So you joined just because
you were invited?

00:02:45.961 --> 00:02:46.621
Yup.

00:02:46.691 --> 00:02:48.461
And because Shino's so nice!

00:02:51.801 --> 00:02:52.701
What about you?

00:02:53.371 --> 00:02:55.131
The same as the girl.

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:56.871
I'm not "the girl".

00:02:57.571 --> 00:03:00.101
My name is Tabby, you know.

00:03:01.141 --> 00:03:05.081
Hey, why did you join the
Twilight Brigade, Sakisaka?

00:03:05.951 --> 00:03:06.571
Me?

00:03:06.981 --> 00:03:07.451
Yes.

00:03:07.651 --> 00:03:08.341
Why did you?

00:03:12.521 --> 00:03:14.681
Is it that hard to remember?

00:03:18.161 --> 00:03:20.421
You had your eye on Shino!

00:03:20.901 --> 00:03:22.021
Nonsense.

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:24.561
Shino's so nice, after all.

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:27.801
I understand how you feel.

00:03:27.871 --> 00:03:29.631
Look, you...

00:03:34.941 --> 00:03:36.041
What are you looking at?

00:03:36.741 --> 00:03:38.271
So, it's you.

00:03:39.681 --> 00:03:41.711
Did you think I was the kid?

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:48.781
I heard he joined
the Twilight Brigade.

00:03:50.331 --> 00:03:54.391
Do you want to go back
to that eccentric man's guild?

00:03:55.101 --> 00:03:56.151
Are you kidding?

00:03:56.761 --> 00:03:59.131
I'm relieved I was able to get out.

00:04:00.001 --> 00:04:01.231
Then, what is it?

00:04:02.001 --> 00:04:06.941
It wasn't like Gord and I
joined because we were invited.

00:04:10.911 --> 00:04:12.211
I just feel...

00:04:15.721 --> 00:04:17.121
...a little disturbed.

00:04:17.691 --> 00:04:19.151
Disturbed?

00:04:20.151 --> 00:04:23.281
It's more like,
I'm jealous of Haseo.

00:04:23.891 --> 00:04:25.831
So you've come to complain.

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:32.921
You're one that never
leaves the Alchemy Area...

00:04:33.301 --> 00:04:35.291
...so there must be something else.

00:04:35.901 --> 00:04:38.171
Maybe I'm imagining things, but...

00:04:40.041 --> 00:04:41.011
I don't know.

00:04:42.841 --> 00:04:44.571
Maybe I'm just tired.

00:04:44.911 --> 00:04:47.781
You're not making yourself
very clear.

00:04:48.151 --> 00:04:50.711
Have there been
a lot of bugs lately?

00:04:52.721 --> 00:04:54.811
Like the graphics distorting...

00:04:54.891 --> 00:04:56.751
...or the sound suddenly cutting off.

00:04:56.821 --> 00:04:58.921
My friend was saying
the same thing.

00:04:59.961 --> 00:05:00.991
Oh...

00:05:01.531 --> 00:05:04.121
With the game turning out
like this...

00:05:04.201 --> 00:05:08.501
...maybe there's no reason to be
worried about bugs anyway.

00:05:08.841 --> 00:05:11.431
Well, there are lots of rumors.

00:05:11.971 --> 00:05:14.411
I wonder what's really going on.

00:05:15.611 --> 00:05:19.441
You think we should really
keep playing here like this?

00:05:20.011 --> 00:05:21.381
Up you go!

00:05:21.851 --> 00:05:22.821
Up you go!

00:05:23.481 --> 00:05:24.181
Up, up!

00:05:26.051 --> 00:05:27.041
Where is he?

00:05:27.891 --> 00:05:30.981
He left while you were
in the bathroom.

00:05:33.431 --> 00:05:34.991
Ovan called him.

00:05:37.671 --> 00:05:39.031
Does that bother you?

00:05:42.001 --> 00:05:43.371
Not really.

00:05:52.081 --> 00:05:55.571
The rumors have really
started to spread.

00:05:55.651 --> 00:05:57.411
Don't worry about that.

00:05:58.391 --> 00:05:59.181
Yes, but...

00:06:00.461 --> 00:06:02.551
Someday someone will realize.

00:06:03.461 --> 00:06:05.051
I know, but...

00:06:06.561 --> 00:06:09.551
How can you stay so calm?

00:06:09.901 --> 00:06:13.631
I wouldn't want to act in haste
and make a mistake.

00:06:16.971 --> 00:06:20.811
Hey, is it really okay for me to
take Haseo to that place?

00:06:21.681 --> 00:06:22.731
I don't mind.

00:06:23.011 --> 00:06:25.101
I wonder if he's already been there.

00:06:25.411 --> 00:06:26.381
That...

00:06:27.581 --> 00:06:29.071
...is a very special place.

00:06:43.061 --> 00:06:44.051
This place?

00:06:45.701 --> 00:06:46.561
It's unusual, isn't it?

00:06:47.601 --> 00:06:48.401
Not really.

00:06:49.941 --> 00:06:51.841
So, what do you want?

00:06:59.251 --> 00:07:00.411
What is that?

00:07:01.021 --> 00:07:03.011
I want you to have this.

00:07:03.321 --> 00:07:04.911
It's a special item.

00:07:06.051 --> 00:07:06.711
For me?

00:07:13.531 --> 00:07:14.321
Don't lose it.

00:07:15.661 --> 00:07:19.221
I said not to receive that order!

00:07:22.841 --> 00:07:24.431
This isn't like you.

00:07:26.541 --> 00:07:30.411
This is the hassle that comes with
having a large guild.

00:07:30.851 --> 00:07:34.371
But, really, there's no order
that you can't take, right?

00:07:35.021 --> 00:07:37.481
If it's rare we can make it
or steal it.

00:07:38.491 --> 00:07:40.251
The Key of the Twilight...

00:07:40.861 --> 00:07:41.321
Huh?

00:07:42.121 --> 00:07:43.111
Haseo...

00:07:43.761 --> 00:07:47.161
Even the core players
are being affected...

00:07:47.231 --> 00:07:49.631
...by the fact that he joined
the Twilight Brigade.

00:07:49.701 --> 00:07:51.961
You mean there are players
that are after it too?

00:07:57.471 --> 00:08:00.411
Then I wonder why
Ovan wants him.

00:08:01.111 --> 00:08:02.301
That Haseo...

00:08:03.341 --> 00:08:05.241
Ask Naobi.

00:08:15.561 --> 00:08:18.531
I want to know
what you're thinking.

00:08:19.291 --> 00:08:21.691
Don't you want someone
more useful?

00:08:22.401 --> 00:08:25.731
A beginner is only
an extra burden.

00:08:27.901 --> 00:08:29.301
Multi-Weapon...

00:08:34.141 --> 00:08:38.581
Do you think we need
an Multi-Weapon to acquire it?

00:08:39.211 --> 00:08:39.981
Well?

00:08:42.081 --> 00:08:44.851
Sure, there aren't many...

00:08:45.951 --> 00:08:48.621
...but I have a few Multi-Weapons
under me.

00:08:49.721 --> 00:08:50.781
That's true.

00:08:51.831 --> 00:08:54.991
But I wonder if it's got to be him
and him alone.

00:08:56.401 --> 00:08:59.491
I'm going to go see what's
going on with our new home.

00:09:03.271 --> 00:09:04.301
Ender...

00:09:07.381 --> 00:09:10.401
Don't take your eyes
off the Twilight Brigade.

00:09:10.981 --> 00:09:11.441
Huh?

00:09:11.951 --> 00:09:13.641
Be extremely cautious.

00:09:13.981 --> 00:09:16.281
Don't miss any information.

00:09:18.391 --> 00:09:19.411
I understand.

00:09:33.471 --> 00:09:34.761
Hurry up!

00:09:35.071 --> 00:09:37.661
There's not much time before
this area's made public!

00:09:39.671 --> 00:09:42.011
Before we know what's going on...

00:09:42.081 --> 00:09:44.371
...we shouldn't act rashly.

00:09:44.711 --> 00:09:50.051
The rumors contain information,
so we should check it out.

00:09:50.281 --> 00:09:53.121
It's important to
enjoy the process.

00:09:53.191 --> 00:09:55.521
So the search shouldn't be forced.

00:09:57.391 --> 00:09:59.121
I'm sick of hearing that.

00:09:59.561 --> 00:10:01.721
That might be true for you.

00:10:02.131 --> 00:10:03.531
Okay! Okay!

00:10:03.601 --> 00:10:05.731
So, what are we supposed to do?

00:10:05.801 --> 00:10:07.531
Should we collect information?

00:10:07.941 --> 00:10:12.201
Tabby, for now you need to
level-up with Sakisaka.

00:10:12.271 --> 00:10:13.211
Okay!

00:10:15.141 --> 00:10:15.441
Let's go!

00:10:15.511 --> 00:10:16.481
Right now?

00:10:17.111 --> 00:10:18.811
Better now than later!

00:10:18.881 --> 00:10:20.571
I don't get it!

00:10:22.721 --> 00:10:24.781
- Hey, wait! Wait a second!
- Come on!

00:10:26.021 --> 00:10:27.111
Bye now!

00:10:29.491 --> 00:10:30.221
What about me?

00:10:30.421 --> 00:10:33.021
You're coming with me.

00:10:33.491 --> 00:10:34.121
Huh?

00:10:34.561 --> 00:10:35.361
What about Ovan?

00:10:36.001 --> 00:10:37.461
I'll join you later.

00:10:38.501 --> 00:10:39.431
Well...

00:10:40.071 --> 00:10:40.971
Shall we go?

00:10:58.221 --> 00:10:59.451
It's big, isn't it?

00:10:59.521 --> 00:11:03.351
This place is different
from the normal area.

00:11:03.921 --> 00:11:05.951
What's the difference?

00:11:28.821 --> 00:11:30.611
Come in!

00:11:39.761 --> 00:11:41.821
So, there are no monsters here?

00:11:41.901 --> 00:11:42.761
That's right.

00:11:49.241 --> 00:11:53.231
There used to be a statue
of a girl here a long time ago.

00:11:54.011 --> 00:11:55.071
A girl?

00:11:56.011 --> 00:11:56.701
Aura.

00:11:57.451 --> 00:11:59.351
That was her name.

00:12:00.211 --> 00:12:02.441
Why isn't she there anymore?

00:12:03.221 --> 00:12:07.881
Well, maybe she just lost
interest in the end...

00:12:08.491 --> 00:12:09.851
...and lost hope for this world.

00:12:10.731 --> 00:12:11.921
What does that mean?

00:12:12.561 --> 00:12:16.831
I mean, what's
the purpose of this area?

00:12:17.061 --> 00:12:18.291
Lost ground.

00:12:18.501 --> 00:12:20.021
Lost what?

00:12:20.571 --> 00:12:21.871
Lost ground.

00:12:22.301 --> 00:12:24.201
A place that cannot be found.

00:12:27.071 --> 00:12:28.671
There are no monsters.

00:12:28.741 --> 00:12:30.971
And even the administrator
can't touch it.

00:12:31.151 --> 00:12:32.271
A mysterious area.

00:12:33.911 --> 00:12:36.041
The Arche Koeln waterfall
is the same.

00:12:36.651 --> 00:12:38.911
You mean that waterfall
we were just at?

00:12:39.091 --> 00:12:39.681
Yes.

00:12:42.821 --> 00:12:44.351
Can't touch it.

00:12:44.761 --> 00:12:46.451
You mean it can't even be erased?

00:12:46.661 --> 00:12:47.561
It seems that way.

00:12:48.231 --> 00:12:52.891
Just when you've forgotten about one,
another is revealed somewhere else.

00:12:53.171 --> 00:12:54.001
Revealed?

00:12:54.271 --> 00:12:57.101
Discovered by a regular player.

00:12:58.511 --> 00:13:00.001
This is a weird game.

00:13:03.881 --> 00:13:04.971
That's right, Haseo.

00:13:05.481 --> 00:13:08.681
This game has
a mysterious autonomy.

00:13:09.581 --> 00:13:10.641
Autonomy?

00:13:12.021 --> 00:13:16.011
Neither the system administrator
nor any outsider can control it.

00:13:16.091 --> 00:13:20.081
Parts of it are controlled
by the rules of the game itself.

00:13:20.391 --> 00:13:21.521
I don't get it.

00:13:25.071 --> 00:13:27.731
In other words,
the Key of the Twilight...

00:13:27.871 --> 00:13:31.301
...is not an item created
by the system administrator.

00:13:31.471 --> 00:13:35.031
It was created by The World itself.

00:13:36.911 --> 00:13:38.441
But, does it...?

00:13:38.511 --> 00:13:39.101
It exists.

00:13:40.151 --> 00:13:42.951
You must play this game with
the assumption that it exists.

00:13:44.551 --> 00:13:47.451
That's why we are
the Twilight Brigade.

00:13:49.291 --> 00:13:50.281
Is it real?

00:13:50.491 --> 00:13:51.081
That's why...

00:13:52.131 --> 00:13:54.291
...it would be exciting
if we found it, right?

00:13:56.261 --> 00:13:56.701
Yeah.

00:14:10.541 --> 00:14:11.531
Excuse me.

00:14:11.611 --> 00:14:14.451
You've been asked to
check out a certain PC.

00:14:21.221 --> 00:14:22.851
You can accept the job.

00:14:23.191 --> 00:14:26.131
But make sure other customers
can't hear.

00:14:26.191 --> 00:14:26.661
Yes.

00:14:27.091 --> 00:14:31.051
And we won't take responsibility
for anything that happens.

00:14:31.871 --> 00:14:34.991
Compensation will be advanced
exactly as the manual says.

00:14:35.071 --> 00:14:35.831
Okay?

00:14:36.201 --> 00:14:36.861
I understand.

00:14:41.511 --> 00:14:41.971
Repth.

00:14:48.281 --> 00:14:49.311
Okay...

00:14:56.891 --> 00:14:59.451
You're climbing the levels
very quickly.

00:15:00.761 --> 00:15:02.191
Not really.

00:15:03.801 --> 00:15:06.461
Maybe it's just because
I'm here to heal you.

00:15:06.531 --> 00:15:07.901
I never asked you to.

00:15:08.901 --> 00:15:09.891
Is that so?

00:15:10.241 --> 00:15:11.971
Okay, I won't do it anymore.

00:15:14.411 --> 00:15:17.241
Hey, don't you think this area
is too tough for me?

00:15:17.681 --> 00:15:21.081
You won't get stronger fighting
something weaker than you.

00:15:21.721 --> 00:15:22.551
Isn't that right?

00:15:23.381 --> 00:15:25.051
I guess so.

00:15:26.951 --> 00:15:27.981
Become stronger.

00:15:30.391 --> 00:15:30.951
Yeah.

00:15:31.461 --> 00:15:32.821
We're going ahead.

00:15:42.371 --> 00:15:44.341
I don't like making things
complicated

00:15:44.411 --> 00:15:46.401
...so I won't beat around the bush.

00:15:47.371 --> 00:15:51.211
Tell me what you know
about the Key of the Twilight.

00:15:52.111 --> 00:15:53.101
I don't know.

00:15:53.351 --> 00:15:54.341
I don't know anything.

00:15:55.251 --> 00:15:57.271
What do you mean
you don't know?

00:15:57.351 --> 00:15:59.181
The Twilight Brigade was...

00:15:59.951 --> 00:16:00.651
Wait!

00:16:01.121 --> 00:16:01.991
Not here.

00:16:04.431 --> 00:16:07.091
I don't want people to know
I was in the Brigade.

00:16:13.171 --> 00:16:16.401
So, why are you, Ender,
from TaN, talking to me?

00:16:18.511 --> 00:16:20.741
You knew and you
still brought me here?

00:16:22.081 --> 00:16:24.771
I just told you
that I don't know anything.

00:16:25.381 --> 00:16:27.371
In fact, I want to ask you
what you know.

00:16:27.881 --> 00:16:30.411
Then how could you have been
in the brigade?

00:16:30.481 --> 00:16:31.781
That's why I left.

00:16:33.491 --> 00:16:34.781
Who knows?

00:16:35.861 --> 00:16:37.981
I don't think anyone knows.

00:16:38.761 --> 00:16:41.461
Even Ovan seemed to be
groping for answers.

00:16:42.801 --> 00:16:44.701
Are you guys idiots?

00:16:45.771 --> 00:16:47.201
Don't count me as one of them.

00:16:47.271 --> 00:16:49.831
I told you, I left.

00:16:51.171 --> 00:16:54.071
If you want to know, why don't
you ask a current member?

00:16:56.941 --> 00:16:58.001
Do you have to go somewhere?

00:16:58.951 --> 00:17:01.351
If we meet in the field,
remember me.

00:17:03.051 --> 00:17:04.181
I'll remember.

00:17:15.901 --> 00:17:16.891
That was scary.

00:17:30.141 --> 00:17:31.511
It's been awhile.

00:17:31.581 --> 00:17:32.241
Hey!

00:17:34.381 --> 00:17:35.541
Hey, Gord!

00:17:37.251 --> 00:17:38.911
You haven't changed!

00:17:40.551 --> 00:17:42.651
Who is this guy?

00:17:44.261 --> 00:17:46.161
This is Gord, a former Brigade member.

00:17:49.661 --> 00:17:51.931
Nice to meet you!
I'm Tabby.

00:17:53.101 --> 00:17:54.591
So you're a newbie.

00:17:54.871 --> 00:17:56.701
What happened with Haseo?

00:18:01.381 --> 00:18:04.171
Why do you know about Haseo?

00:18:04.811 --> 00:18:05.681
I met him.

00:18:06.051 --> 00:18:08.451
We talked about the brigade.

00:18:09.421 --> 00:18:11.541
Are you Haseo's friend?

00:18:12.421 --> 00:18:12.941
No.

00:18:13.221 --> 00:18:15.481
He's kind of like my pupil.

00:18:16.121 --> 00:18:17.021
Pupil?

00:18:17.321 --> 00:18:20.291
We can take the time
to talk about it later.

00:18:20.361 --> 00:18:22.351
I have to be somewhere.
I'm off.

00:18:23.631 --> 00:18:24.891
See ya!

00:18:29.041 --> 00:18:31.661
Haseo seems to have
a lot of connections.

00:18:32.471 --> 00:18:33.671
What about you?

00:18:33.941 --> 00:18:34.411
Huh?

00:18:34.841 --> 00:18:36.071
You have connections?

00:18:37.181 --> 00:18:42.381
Um, Sakisaka
and Shino and...

00:18:42.451 --> 00:18:44.111
I'm part of it, huh.

00:18:49.061 --> 00:18:50.461
How annoying.

00:18:51.021 --> 00:18:53.221
What exactly is Haseo?

00:18:55.931 --> 00:18:59.961
This is really annoying!
What's so special about him?

00:19:01.031 --> 00:19:04.001
I'm special, too!

00:19:05.441 --> 00:19:08.201
Why are we the only ones
that have to level up?

00:19:08.281 --> 00:19:09.331
Who cares?

00:19:10.081 --> 00:19:13.981
I bet you Haseo has gone off
somewhere else with Ovan.

00:19:15.621 --> 00:19:16.671
Without us.

00:19:17.451 --> 00:19:18.351
Are you serious?

00:19:18.991 --> 00:19:19.981
For real?

00:19:20.451 --> 00:19:22.891
We've been brushed aside.

00:19:23.891 --> 00:19:26.051
Shino's not like that.

00:19:28.301 --> 00:19:30.061
You just don't get it.

00:19:30.131 --> 00:19:33.431
Why do I have to be
stuck with this?

00:19:34.131 --> 00:19:35.861
Don't say "this"!

00:19:44.181 --> 00:19:44.801
You're late.

00:19:46.651 --> 00:19:48.051
Sorry. Sorry.

00:19:48.521 --> 00:19:51.921
You called me out and you're late.
Who do you think you are?

00:19:59.961 --> 00:20:01.431
Backdoor work.

00:20:01.831 --> 00:20:02.851
What kind?

00:20:03.501 --> 00:20:05.021
The usual.

00:20:05.631 --> 00:20:07.931
Investigate without being caught.

00:20:08.641 --> 00:20:09.731
What about compensation?

00:20:10.101 --> 00:20:12.401
Unfortunately, our guild
does not have...

00:20:12.471 --> 00:20:17.431
...the wonderful system of personally
advancing compensation.

00:20:18.051 --> 00:20:21.501
Even though my account
might be suspended?

00:20:22.581 --> 00:20:23.881
That's work.

00:20:27.391 --> 00:20:28.381
And...

00:20:29.421 --> 00:20:30.011
What?

00:20:30.421 --> 00:20:33.221
Warn the people that are
making it...

00:20:33.291 --> 00:20:35.521
...that the distribution
has become too large.

00:20:36.301 --> 00:20:38.261
Isn't it supply and demand?

00:20:38.831 --> 00:20:40.891
In principle.

00:20:41.241 --> 00:20:43.071
But we can't be too visible.

00:20:43.471 --> 00:20:46.131
We did get this huge building.

00:20:47.141 --> 00:20:50.771
I'll tell them, but they're not
the types that listen very well.

00:20:51.181 --> 00:20:53.651
It's all up to your skills.

00:20:54.351 --> 00:20:55.181
Yeah. Yeah.

00:21:07.531 --> 00:21:08.821
Where are Ovan and Shino?

00:21:09.861 --> 00:21:11.161
They went somewhere.

00:21:11.801 --> 00:21:12.701
Oh.

00:21:18.671 --> 00:21:22.041
What were you doing
before you came here?

00:21:23.241 --> 00:21:24.401
What do you mean?

00:21:25.011 --> 00:21:26.641
You met Gord, right?

00:21:27.151 --> 00:21:27.911
Why?

00:21:28.381 --> 00:21:29.311
No reason.

00:21:32.021 --> 00:21:33.041
No reason?

00:21:34.291 --> 00:21:36.721
I won't let you get off that easily.

00:21:38.261 --> 00:21:39.621
What are you trying to do?

00:21:40.131 --> 00:21:42.601
What did you come here for?

00:21:44.261 --> 00:21:45.321
It has nothing to do with you.

00:21:46.071 --> 00:21:48.861
I'm a member
of the Twilight Brigade.

00:21:48.941 --> 00:21:50.461
Of course, it has something
to do with me.

00:21:52.111 --> 00:21:54.731
It's just a game.
Cool off.

00:21:58.881 --> 00:21:59.901
Why, you!

00:22:08.721 --> 00:22:09.621
Tabby...

00:22:10.721 --> 00:22:12.091
...got PK'd!

00:22:30.041 --> 00:22:33.641
Ikiru wa dokuhai kiyu no kurushimi wo
Life is a poisoned cup of needless suffering

00:22:33.711 --> 00:22:37.151
Nomihosu sube wo dare ga sazukeyo
That no one can show me how to drain

00:22:37.421 --> 00:22:41.151
Taiyo ni sumu toiu kenja no washi
A wise eagle is said to live in the sun

00:22:41.221 --> 00:22:45.251
Habataki dake ga kodama suru
The flapping of its wings
is all that echoes

00:22:48.761 --> 00:22:52.361
Kono futatsu no me ni yadotta
In each of these eyes

00:22:52.431 --> 00:22:56.061
Yami to Hikari sono docchi de
Dwell darkness and light

00:22:56.141 --> 00:23:03.371
Boku wa ashita wo mitsumeru beki nano darou
Through which shall I look to tomorrow?

00:23:03.441 --> 00:23:07.111
Kawaki kitta gareki no machi
A dried out and ruined city

00:23:07.181 --> 00:23:10.881
Ten to sen wo tsunagi awase
Draws the lines between the dots

00:23:10.951 --> 00:23:17.881
Imi nado nai koto bakari afurete iku
Causing meaningless events to overflow

00:23:18.061 --> 00:23:21.791
Honou no gotoki kodoku
Soothing the loneliness

00:23:21.861 --> 00:23:24.891
Idaku karada shizumete wa
That flames up within the body

00:23:24.971 --> 00:23:32.431
Ankyo eto shitatatte iku shizuku
Droplets of water fall towards the culvert

00:23:32.671 --> 00:23:35.871
Kakageru dokuhai kono sei wa michitemo
Even if the poisoned cup is upheld
and filled with this life

00:23:35.941 --> 00:23:39.971
Kogareru shino yume wa nagare tsuku
My dream that yearns for death
drifts into it

00:23:40.081 --> 00:23:43.681
Toride ni kuikomu tsume kokou no washi
The eagle remains aloof;
its talons dig into the fort

00:23:43.751 --> 00:23:47.311
Habataki dake ga maiagaru
Only the flapping of its wings resounds

00:23:47.391 --> 00:23:51.121
Ano soukyu ni takkei ni shite kure tamae
Let me be crucified in the blue sky

00:23:51.191 --> 00:23:54.891
Ten to chi ga musubu basho ni
bokuwa tatsu
I'll stand where heaven and earth meet

00:23:56.031 --> 00:23:57.521
Next Episode...
